Send a POST body without a type as it is, not as a form.

curl labels every POST body application/x-www-form-urlencoded unless the
request names a type; the port removed that label only for empty bodies. A
fetch() or XMLHttpRequest body made of a Blob or an ArrayBuffer has no type,
and servers then parsed the bytes as a form (httpbin.org showed an empty body).
Now no Content-Type is sent unless the request has one, as other browsers do.

diff --git a/Source/WebCore/platform/network/curl/CurlRequest.cpp b/Source/WebCore/platform/network/curl/CurlRequest.cpp
index f5cdbf6..31abb87 100644
--- a/Source/WebCore/platform/network/curl/CurlRequest.cpp
+++ b/Source/WebCore/platform/network/curl/CurlRequest.cpp
@@ -563,8 +563,10 @@ void CurlRequest::setupPOST()
     m_curlHandle->enableHttpPostRequest(totalSize);
     m_curlHandle->setReadCallbackFunction(willSendDataCallback, this);
 
-    // Override the default POST Content-Type: header
-    if (!m_request.hasHTTPHeader(HTTPHeaderName::ContentType) && !totalSize)
+    // curl labels every POST body application/x-www-form-urlencoded unless told
+    // otherwise; a body sent without a type (a Blob or buffer) goes without one,
+    // as in other browsers.
+    if (!m_request.hasHTTPHeader(HTTPHeaderName::ContentType))
         m_curlHandle->removeRequestHeader("Content-Type"_s);
 
     // Disable a "Expect: 100-continue" header
